course: dictionary
lesson: 7125
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word pelt can be a noun, a thing, or a verb, an action. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «Beaver pelts were traded by fur traders in Canada.» Here a pelt is an animal's skin with the fur still on. Now read «It's pelting down, so grab your coat.» Nobody is throwing anything. Pelting here means the rain is falling very hard.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your chosen meaning into the sentence in place of the word and check that it makes sense. If it does not, try another meaning.
fact: Pelt can be a noun: the skin of an animal with the fur or hair still on.
fact: Pelt can be a verb: to throw many things at someone quickly, as in «pelt with snowballs».
fact: «It's pelting down» means the rain or hail is falling very hard.
fact: «At full pelt» means as fast as possible, as in «He pelted down the road».
fact: A word with several meanings is hard to guess alone, so use the other words in the sentence to decide.
exercise: «Beaver pelts were traded by fur traders in Canada long ago.» What is a pelt here? | A wooden boat | *The skin of an animal, with the fur still on | A type of cloud | A kind of hat
exercise: «It's pelting down, so grab your coat.» What does pelting mean? | Shining brightly | Throwing things at people | *Raining very hard | Running very fast
exercise: «He ran down the road at full pelt.» What does at full pelt mean? | *As fast as possible | In a full bag | Very slowly | Without any clothes
test: «The children pelted each other with snowballs in the playground.» What does pelted mean here? | Sang loudly | *Threw many things quickly at each other | Fell very softly | Slept in the snow
test: «Hailstones pelted down on the car roof all afternoon.» What does pelted down mean? | *Fell very hard | Turned into snow | Floated gently | Walked slowly
exam: «The crowd pelted Toad with carrots, and he was far from happy.» What does pelted mean here? | Gently gave | *Threw many things at him quickly | Painted | Hugged
